+/// How long implicit/explicit activation waits for a spawned service to
+/// actually appear in the name registry before giving up.
+///
+/// The D-Bus spec leaves this to the implementation (the reference
+/// `dbus-daemon` defaults to 25s). We pick something much shorter because
+/// LeandrOS activation targets are local, statically-linked binaries with
+/// no dynamic loader/network startup cost, and a hung activation attempt
+/// otherwise blocks the calling peer's connection for the full timeout.
+const ACTIVATION_TIMEOUT: Duration = Duration::from_secs(5);
+
+/// Poll interval while waiting for an activated service to claim its name.
+/// There's no notification hook into `NameRegistry` to await instead, so
+/// this is a plain poll loop; see `Peers::await_name_owner`.
+const ACTIVATION_POLL_INTERVAL: Duration = Duration::from_millis(50);
